@graywolf336 reported an issue where he tried to clear the width/height values, and the web UI sent empty strings.  Obviously the backend isn't expecting strings for a number value, so errors were thrown.  I could just fix this on the frontend, but given the API is open it's best to defensively handle this so anybody else who might send an empty string or a nil value won't get an error.

However, this feels like overkill.  @graywolf336 @muesli @geekgonecrazy do you have any other solutions to unmarshalling unexpected types that's better than manually handling the cases?

Closes #781

